      "note": "\u26a0\ufe0f ASYMMETRIC BRIDGE. Ethereum's pool (0xa0de671e\u20260d86) is CCIP LockReleaseTokenPool 1.6.1; the BSC pool (0x904939a9\u20260c61) is BurnWithFromMintTokenPool 1.6.1. Ethereum LOCKS and the destination MINTS, so Ethereum's totalSupply already contains the bridged portion and summing the chains would DOUBLE-COUNT it. An earlier version of this field published such a sum, having read the BSC pool's type and assumed Ethereum's. ethereum_locked_in_bridge_pool is the part of Ethereum supply that no account holds. Global circulating supply is UNRESOLVED. TO ESTABLISH IT: reconcile every destination chain's minted supply against this pool's locked balance \u2014 two chain selectors are configured and only one is identified, and the locked balance far exceeds the known remote mints, which is either more destinations or liquidity provided for return trips."
